From ed725f5f54703faace9854d0b829c68994222533 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:43:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(motion): the rotary wrap closes a flatted bar's
 ragged seam and refuses an open mesh by name

The developed sheet's two free ends were closed by a meridian wall standing
in the plane of the cover's extreme column. On a revolve the seam column is
straight and lies in that plane; on a bar with a D-flat across the seam the
flat's vertices sit at their own azimuths, the seam column is ragged, and the
wall met none of its edges - "the mesh is open: 4/8/16 dangling chord ends".

Now each seam edge (an edge its two facets develop one period apart) hangs a
vertical curtain down to the floor radius from its lower (first copy) and its
upper (second copy) version - multiaxis::rotary_seam. On a revolve that is
the old wall, split on the same diagonal: the OffsetRings wrap digest is
unchanged. The wrap also refuses an open mesh by name before developing it;
on main a hole no ladder level sliced through wrapped silently.

Pinned by rotary_dflat::{a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement,
a_bar_with_a_hole_in_its_skin_is_still_refused_by_name,
a_flat_channel_across_the_seam_is_refused_adaptive_by_name_and_rings_cut_it}
(all three fail on main), the last being #9's seam law end to end.

Fixes #54

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
